lack's winning chances go from 40% to 9%.","points":["White answers 55.Kh5.","Better was 54…Qc1 (+1.11): shores up the h6 pawn, which was under as much attack as it had defence (1 against 1)."],"better":"54…Qc1 shores up the h6 pawn. Engine line: 55.Qd6+ Kg8 56.Qg6 Qb2 57.Qe6+ Kh7 (+1.11)."},{"ply":119,"name":"60.Qc8+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"60.Qc8+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Moves the attacked queen to safety.","Check, and Black has only one legal reply.","The next best move, 60.Qd6+, would drop White's winning chances from 98% to 50% (0.00).","60.Qc8+ saves the attacked queen and gives check, leaving one reply.","Black answers 60…Qe8.","After 60…Qe8 61.Qxe8+ Kxe8 62.Kg7 Kd7 63.f7, the queens come off (+10.16)."]}],"opening":{"name":"Bishop's Opening: Paulsen Defense","eco":"C24","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 10.Na3: 19 moves in all, 10 by White and 9 by Black.","Theory runs out after 10.Na3: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}